			"notes": "I worked on movement speed as I was informed that it was quite weird. It's a bit difficult to pull off since Cobblemon have a weird relationship with the speed attribute. Instead of trying to make all pokemon use the same speed when they have the same stats, it now uses the actual movement speed of the pokemon normally with a modifier to slow them down if their speed is low. Feedback about it would be very welcome, I might tweak it in the upcoming days/weeks to get it to a good point.\n\nThis does end up having weird interactions such as a Regirock with 50 speed being faster than a Pikachu with 100 speed, but Pikachu does have a slower movement speed than Regirock which is why that occurs. This might change up the meta as far as which pokemon are viable for melee attacks, but it should be more easy to predict now at least. No more Geodudes racing around at top speed."
		},
